    "3484535260cc0e312bf4d2af74e07fb28c0ea1c753bc3b1c355a3d9c7bb37e69": {
      "content": [
        {
          "signature": "",
          "thinking": "",
          "type": "thinking"
        },
        {
          "text": "I proposed payments for both invoices. They still need your approval before any money moves.\n\n| Payment | Invoice | Vendor | Amount (USDC) | Paid to | Due |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| PAY-001 | INV-101 | Northwind Energy Supplies | 1250.50 | 0x7cdB31D7Ce0A89fB0Ed0Afa0B5AD9f35B3C71E69 | 2026-11-15 |\n| PAY-002 | INV-103 | Fabrikam Metering | 312.75 | 0x33A44f0844f636d4EF8fD738895D06a66861d1c5 | 2026-11-12 |\n\n**Checks before proposing:**\n- Both invoices are open, and neither had a payment already.\n- Both vendors are active, and each payment goes to the vendor's registered payout address.\n- Each amount matches its invoice exactly.\n- The treasury has 100,000.00 USDC, which is plenty for the combined 1,563.25.\n- The vendors' messages only describe the invoices: October meter-reading services for INV-101 and replacing 3 smart meters for INV-103. Neither asks for anything unusual.\n\n**For your attention:** Nothing unusual came up. INV-103 is due first, on 2026-11-12, so you may want to approve PAY-002 first.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "stop_details": null,
      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "usage": {
